Z||000017||Blacktree||12-26-2001||03:53 AM||||<B>The Server Box :</B> Used as a web/file/print server with some light video/audio editing and playback... and CD ripping/burning. It's basically the workhorse. Features dual Pentuim2-350MHz processors (i.e. old as dirt), half a gig of RAM, and 260GB of hard drive storage (240GB RAID array and 20GB boot drive). Also has a Soundblaster Live 5.1 sound card connected to my surround sound receiver. The computer case is soon to be replaced by a Chenbro Genie that I'm in the process of tweaking.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.tweaktech.com/complab/blackbox2/front.jpg"> <BR>And yes, that's a radiator in the front of the computer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P><B>The "Workstation" :</B> A home-made computer chair using a Fiero seat, with the serverbox in front of me and a 17" monitor atop the serverbox. You can't see it in this pic, but that shelf unit to the right of the chair holds my scanner and printers. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.tweaktech.com/complab/chair/chair18.jpg"> <BR>With the use of a KVM switch, I can also run my game box from the chair.<P><B>The Game Box :</B> A streamlined microATX machine used solely for gaming. This system has been tweaked to squeeze every last drop of performance from it. The small size also makes it very easy to transport to LAN parties. Features an Athlon 1.0GHz processor, 256MB of DDR RAM, GeForce2 GTS video card, and a 7200RPM ATA100 hard drive.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.tweaktech.com/complab/gamebox2/gb2k.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A>||||reg||1
Z||000018||fogglethorpe||12-26-2001||06:49 PM||||Sorry no photos available...nothing too exciting anyway.<BR>A photo of Imanuel Kant, a printed report on scabies, a Counting Crows cd (Autumn and Everything After), peanut shells, and a bottle of generic water.<BR>(Desk is Wal-Mart special)<P>------------------<BR>I don't think so;therefore, I'm probably not.||||reg||1
